- Object formats: AnnData `.h5ad` for Python (scanpy) and `.rds` for R (Seurat/SingleCellExperiment). Convert with a recorded tool and version; do not keep two hand-maintained copies.
- Name objects by stage: `results/objects/<stage>.h5ad` (or `.rds`), e.g. `01-qc`, `02-normalized`, `03-integrated`, `04-annotated`.
- Store raw counts in the object (`layers["counts"]` / `counts` assay) alongside normalized values.
